.TH ARIA_MOVE 1 "October 2026" "aria_move 1.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aria_move \- safely move completed aria2 downloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aria_move
.RI [ options ] " source"
.br
.B aria_move
.RI [ options ] " gid num_files source"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Moves a completed file or download directory, preserving existing destinations.
Uses atomic rename on one filesystem and verified copies across filesystems.
Refuses symlinks and unfinished downloads.
The Debian service runs aria2 under the aria-move account and invokes this
executable directly on completion.
.SH SOURCE SELECTION
Explicit source paths and single-file aria2 hooks move only that entry.
Multi-file aria2 downloads must have their own top-level folder below
download_base; the hook's first-file path selects that folder.
Use --source-path with an exact folder for other layouts.
Completed .tmp, .part and .crdownload files are accepted.
Aria2 control files still prevent a move.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show all supported options.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Select configuration; overrides ARIA_MOVE_CONFIG and default paths.
.TP
.B --print-config
Print the selected configuration path.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate configuration without creating storage directories or moving files.
Does not test write access.
.TP
.B --init --download-base PATH --completed-base PATH
Create configuration exclusively; never overwrites an existing file.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Report a move without changing downloads.
.TP
.B --preserve-metadata
Preserve permissions, timestamps and supported extended attributes when copying.
.TP
.B --preserve-permissions
Preserve permissions when copying.
.TP
.B --disable-locks
Disable per-download locks for filesystems without lock support.
.TP
.BI --log-level " LEVEL"
Log file contents: warn (default; warnings and errors), normal (completed moves,
warnings and errors) or verbose (everything).
.TP
.B --json
Write the log file as JSON lines.
.SH LOGGING
Application warnings, errors and crashes always go to the system log
(syslog, identifier aria_move; view with journalctl -t aria_move) and stderr,
whatever the log level. The log file receives only what the log level selects.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/aria_move/config.xml
Packaged mover configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/aria_move/aria2.conf
Packaged aria2 configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/aria-move
Managed incoming/completed downloads, session and private RPC token.
.TP
.I /var/log/aria-move
Move logs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; nonzero for invalid arguments, incomplete setup or move failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aria2c (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.br
